<p>By CMG Lee, a pleasing visual proof that the number of possible handshakes among <em>n</em> people is the (<em>n</em>-1)th triangular number.</p>
<p>The first pair shake hands, and each new arrival shakes with everyone already present. The cumulative total counts every possible handshake.</p>
